From 6a7227559bed3173d813b360091fb33bdba80ab1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PyScotch <pyscotch@noreply.invalid>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 13:06:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 08/11] Bugfix: match geometry data against node labels in
 `meshGeomLoadScot()` [report R. Perry]

`meshGeomLoadScot()` took the node labels from `vlbltax[baseval ..]`,
that is, from the first vertices of the mesh, which are elements when
elements are numbered first; coordinates were then matched against
element labels ("vertex geometry data not found", or misplaced
coordinates). For unlabeled meshes it expected the labels 0 .. vnodnbr-1
whereas `meshGeomSaveScot()` writes the node numbers vnodbas ..
vnodnnd-1. Like its graph twin, it also kept the geometry dimension in
a local, so `SCOTCH_geomData()` reported dimension 0 and
`meshGeomSaveScot()` wrote no coordinates, and it reused a pre-existing
`geomtab` without checking its size.

Index labels from `vnodbas` and use node numbers as labels for
unlabeled meshes, (re)allocate `geomtab` to the proper size, record
the dimension and print the missing label with the proper format.

Add `test_scotch_mesh_geom`, which loads a mesh and its geometry,
checks them and writes the geometry back for comparison.

Refs: SEP-16, GRA-09
